We finished the finals in 12th place. In the qualifier round, we finished 6th place. The judges gave vague feedback for the qualifier round, and did the same for the finale. After going to the competition, I realized that it is just a game of nepotism. Many teams had classes, like class periods in school, dedicated to just the competition, and some even had actual Future City coaches and and accompanying professional level models and pamphlets, likely sourced from their connections over the many years Future City has been running. Even though we didn't really stand a chance with people who had already snowballed their way to the top, I am proud of how far we got with just afterschool work hours. I didn't do much of the design for the solutions, but I know for a fact that we did not have a chunk of our school day allocated for it. Basically, we did more with less, so my ego is satisfied. In conclusion, I will no longer be doing Future City because of this nepotism. Also because my friends aren't participating either.

